<!-- Ўзбекча (кирилл): the libraries' own texts (i18n.md §1.4.6; build plan 6.3b). appcompat, Compose
     and androidx.biometric ship values-uz and values-ru but no Cyrillic Uzbek, so without this file
     their texts appear in English while the app is in Ўзбекча. An app string with a library string's
     name wins when resources are merged; tools:override="true" marks each as deliberate.

     The names are those that reach the merged release APK (`aapt2 dump resources` on
     app-release-unsigned.apk, built at wave-6A-merged + part b; resources shrunk by R8), with each
     library's own values-uz text converted by UzbekCyrillicStrings (i18n.md §2.5) and read against it:
     - material3-android 1.4.0: m3c_*, the labels TalkBack reads for sheets, dialogs, menus, snackbars;
     - ui-android 1.12.1: the states and roles TalkBack reads (on, off, selected, tab, switch…);
     - foundation-android 1.12.1: the text field's menu (autofill) and tooltips;
     - biometric 1.4.0-alpha07: the fingerprint dialog the library draws itself on Android 7 to 8.1
       (API 24 to 27) and its messages.
     Not overridden: appcompat 1.8.0's 20 abc_* strings in the APK (action bar, search view, menu
     shortcuts, SwitchCompat's ON/OFF), which no screen shows: the screens are Compose, and the
     window has no action bar. androidx_startup is not translatable.

     Make this list again whenever one of these libraries changes version, and remove a name that
     no longer reaches the merged APK (i18n.md §1.4.6). -->
